node_definition.done_when:
Prototype and measure a fixed-shape lean forward map and its converged solve, and find the smallest cell count that passes the section 6 acceptance. Lead ruling 2026-10-14: the lean map is the direction, but every shape must stay fixed so solves batch and vmap. The cell count is set by section 6 accuracy alone: map fidelity at most 1e-2 relative sup, and roots within one pitch.

Why. docs/research/forward-solve-options.html (merged at 44816b793) measured no route under 1 ms. The dense map carries 6 Bell jet components per node, about 3.45 nodes per cell and 3 moments per cell, which is about 62 entries per cell pair: 2.2 GB at 2,098 cells and 12.7 GB at 5,167. Reading it alone has a floor near 0.5 and 2.6 ms. Exact booking costs 26 to 229 ms. The live residual measured 1.1 s against about 47 ms of measured parts. Meanwhile exact booking already reaches 4.7e-6 limited and 1.8e-5 diverted map error at about 2,000 cells, 500 to 2,000 times inside the 1e-2 ceiling. So the grids are far finer than section 6 needs.

Done when one research document, docs/research/fixed-shape-lean-map.html (reckon-type research, plan-informs converged-forward-solve), reports measurements from prototypes under scripts/prototypes/lean_map:

(0) Explain the point-booking bias first. The hard-centroid diverted map error is 0.42 to 0.43 and does not fall from 2,000 to 10,000 cells; the limited one stalls at 3.6e-3. Find the cause, for example private-flux cells below the X-point counted inside, a missing connected-component test, or a normalisation or area error. Show the corrected interior quadrature converging with refinement.

(1) A fixed-shape lean map, all shapes static for a given machine:
- a dense precomputed values map from cell sources to flux at every cell's interior quadrature points;
- the full six-jet node map, stored but read only through a fixed-capacity row gather for the boundary band and the fixed-point windows. The capacity is chosen per machine with a stated margin, and an over-capacity state returns a typed refusal, as fixed_points does with NEEDS_ROWS;
- exact booking for cut cells in a fixed-capacity batch;
- Gauss-point booking inside.
Measure whether one current per interior cell suffices or first moments are needed, and report what it costs in accuracy.

(2) Converged solve on that map: Newton on the cell sources with the Jacobian route that is fastest at these sizes. Measure dense jacfwd over all columns under vmap, and a cached factor for warm slices. Report:
- cold and warm converged walls on the H200;
- batched throughput per slice under jax.vmap at batch widths 1, 16 and 128, with identical shapes across the batch;
- the map evaluation wall against its memory-bandwidth floor;
- JVP against finite differences;
- what the two production zero-current seeds do.

(3) Cell-count ladder at about 250, 500, 1,000 and 2,000 cells on the analytic limited and diverted certificates. Report map fidelity and converged flux error against the analytic solution, and axis and X-point distance in pitches. Name the smallest count passing section 6 with at least a tenfold margin (map error at most 1e-3), and state its converged warm and cold walls against the 1 ms target.

Build the coarse certificate carriers with NOVA_ANALYTIC_ORACLE_BUILDER=device into this run's own directory. Never write the certified caches.

Figures go under docs/figures/converged-forward-solve/lean-map. Plot wall and error against cells (one canvas each). Draw one poloidal panel per topology at the chosen count showing the band and cut cells, following AGENTS.md plotting rules. reckon audit-doc must report 0 errors.

This is a prototype and measurement node. Do not change nova/ product code, and do not touch the held moment-space Newton worktree (read it only). Reuse nova.media.ink for figure styling rather than restyling. Write an evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/converged-forward-solve/lean-map.html with plan-evidence-for converged-forward-solve that anchors the headline numbers.

Run conditions: H200 rows run as one job through RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 scripts/h200_test_lane/run.sh --log (an absolute path in the run directory) --wait -- (targets), or one sbatch job on --partition=betelgeuse --reservation=gpu_0003_grpA --gres=gpu:1 with rungs as rows inside the allocation (never an array), --time sized to finish, XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_PREALLOCATE=false and TMPDIR=/tmp in the submit environment and in every child; submit for real and read squeue a minute later rather than trusting sbatch --test-only. On a compute node run /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python directly with PYTHONPATH set to the run worktree and never invoke uv; every login-node uv command carries --no-sync and nothing runs uv sync. configure_dtypes() before any array and jax_enable_x64 asserted True. Gates pass by delta against orientation_base_sha in per-module fresh processes, both arms running the same test files with the repository root conftest, baseline_suite and after_suite as single-line JSON whose log_path names one log file and whose command is literally runnable. Any wait is declared on the job that finishes last as wait_probe ["sacct","-n","-X","-P","-j","(job id)","-o","State"] and wait_terminal ["COMPLETED","FAILED","CANCELLED","TIMEOUT","OUT_OF_MEMORY","NODE_FAIL"] as JSON lists, and names every job it depends on in wait_condition. The certified 550, 2,000 and 5,000-cell machines and exteriors are cached under /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/runs/r-20261009T181553786165-proto-support/ordered/rows/cache and may be read in place, never written. Run filepath relativize over any evidence fragment before committing. Commit with conventional subjects and bodies at every step and write the manifest and commit before every job wait; the manifest commits line lists every commit; status is complete, blocked or failed, which the worker sets itself. No plan labels in source names or comments.

Import provenance: print nova.__file__ in every log header. On the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set), run CPU work in place. The time budget is per working turn, not a deadline: park on H200 jobs with declared waits and continue across turns; this node is sized at about 6 worker-hours. Size every job memory from a measured row, never a guess. The manifest commits line lists every commit (git rev-list), orientation_base_sha is copied from git rev-parse output, and status is complete, blocked or failed.

